        "text": "15.2 OSMOREGULATION\n\nChapter 15\n\nA type of homeostasis in which water and ions (electrolytes) concentration is maintained in the cells and in the intercellular fluids is called osmoregulation. Balance of water and electrolytes is very critical to the health of animals. The mechanisms involved in regulating water and electrolytes balance vary widely among the animal groups as different habitats present different challenges.",
