        "headingUrdu": "موضوع 7",
        "text": "15.2.2 Osmoregulators\n\nSome animals like all land animals and most marine vertebrates have body fluids whose solute concentration is different from that of the external environment. Therefore they must use energy in controlling water loss or gain to keep the balance of water and solutes. Such animals are called osmoregulators. Whether an animal inhabits land, fresh water or salt water, its cells cannot survive without water.",
