        "text": "15.2.3 Osmoconformers\n\nSome aquatic animals that live in the sea have the body fluids with a solute concentration equal to that of external environment. Such animals do not undergo a net gain or loss of water because equal amounts of water move back and forth between two solutions with equal solute concentration i.e. the animal body fluids are kept isotonic. Such animals are called osmoconformers.",
