        "headingUrdu": "موضوع 14",
        "text": "15.4.1 Ammonia\n\nChapter 15\n\nAmmonia is highly toxic and highly soluble in water. 1 g of nitrogen, in the form of ammonia, requires 500 ml of water to dissolve it to nontoxic level. If the organism has a sufficient source of water, ammonia can simply be excreted out. This is the course taken by many aquatic organisms, particularly those in fresh water.\n\nAnimals which excrete ammonia as their major nitrogenous waste product are called ammonotelic e.g. most fishes, protozoans, sponges, coelenterates, echinoderms.",
