        "text": "17.5.2 Central Nervous System:\n\nParasympathetic Division (dominates during times of \"rest and rumination\"; directs\n\nmaintenance activities)\n\nCentral nervous system consists of brain and spinal cord, both act as coordinating centers, but brain is involved more in coordination than spinal cord. Spinal cord also acts as a link between PNS and brain.",
