          "The somatic system is the part of the peripheral nervous system responsible for carrying sensory and motor information between CNS and voluntary parts of the body. The somatic nervous system controls skeletal muscle as well as external sensory organs such as the skin. This system is said to be voluntary because the responses can be controlled consciously. Reflex reactions of skeletal muscle however are an exception. These are involuntary reactions to external stimuli."
