        "text": "20.3 MENSTRUAL CYCLE\n\nThe reproductive cycle in human and other primates is called menstrual cycle. The first menstruation begins at puberty. The uterine or menstrual cycle is a series of cyclic changes that the uterine endometrium goes through each month as it responds to the waxing and waning of ovarian hormones in the blood. These endometrial changes are coordinated with the phases of the ovarian cycle, which are controlled by gonadotropins released by the anterior pituitary.\n\nVarious phases of menstrual cycle are as follows:",
