          "It is believed that the modern concept of gene was given by the Mendel while his experimentation on pea plant. According to the Mendel, each trait in the pea plant is controlled by the discrete units, what he referred as elementen or factors. In modern terminology Mendel's factors are called genes. Since the rediscovery of Mendelian work in 1900, the nature and expression of gene is being explored by various geneticists in all over the world and this job is still continued. But now we know that a gene is composed of nucleotide sequence of a short segment of DNA which encodes the sequence of amino acid of a particular polypeptide. 23.2.3 Where do genes reside?",
