        "heading": "23.5.4 Meselson-Stahl Experiment:",
        "headingUrdu": "موضوع 18",
        "text": "23.5.4 Meselson-Stahl Experiment:\n\nThe three models of DNA replication were evaluated by Mathew Meselson and Franklin Stahl of the California Institute of technology in 1958. In this experiment, it was concluded finally that the replication of DNA occurs according to semi-conservative model.\n\nawaz e inqilab.com\n\nChromosomes and DNA\n\nCulturing Urbeterth\n\nChapter 23\n\nThey grew bacteria in a medium containing heavy isotope of nitrogen, \"N, which became incorporated into the bases of bacterial DNA. After several generations, the bacteria were shifted to three separate plates, which were already contained \"N medium.\n\nSampling TBXX\n\nThree DNA samples were taken from bacteria shifted from \"N medium to the \"N medium. First sample was obtained from first plate just after the transfer of culture; called sample at 0 minute, the second sample was taken from second plate after 20 minutes, called sample at 20 minutes, and third sample was taken from third plate after another 20 minute, called sample at 40 minute. In addition to these, a control sample was also taken from the bacteria which were grown separately in \"N\n\nmedium.\n\nCenfrigation of DNX\n\nres\n\nThe DNA samples were dissolved in cesium chloride (CSCI) solution and then spun at a very high speed in an ultra-centrifuge for many hours. The cesium and chloride ions tend to be pushed by centrifugal force towards the bottom of the tube.\n\nDNA Bacterial cell\n\nSample at\n\n0 minutes\n\nBacteria grown in\n\nmedium containing heavy isotope of nitrogen\n\nSample al 20 minutes\n\nAllow to grow\n\nIn medium\n\ncontaining Eight isotope of nitrogen\n\nSample at 40 minutes\n\nBreak open cells and extract DNA\n\nSuspended DNA In cesium chloride solution\n\nCentrifugation\n\nControl group Labeled parent (Unlabeled DNA) (both strands\n\nheavy)\n\nF1 generation F2 generation DNA DNA( one heatyne labeled molecule light hybrid and heavy light hybrid molecule) molecule).\n\nFig:23.7\n\nChromosomes and DNA\n\nResults ofcentrifugation\n\nChapter 23\n\nDNA of control sample was appeared lightest as formed sediment at the top of test tube, while DNA of sample at 0 minute was appeared heaviest as it formed sediment at the bottom of test tube. The DNA of sample at 20 minute formed sediment intermediate level to that of control sample and sample at 0 minute whereas sample at 40 minute had two sediments, one at the top and other at intermediate level.\n\nInterpretations of resuks\n\nTop of centrifuge tube\n\n14N Hybrid\n\nאיי\n\nMeselson-Stahl interpreted their results as (Lower density) follows: the DNA of control sample appeared lightest because it had both strands of \"N, whereas DNA of sample at 0 minute appeared heaviest because it had both strand of \"N, but after first round of replication each daughter duplex was a hybrid possessing one strand of \"N and one of \"N so it formed sediment at intermediate level.\n\nBottom of ccentrifuge tube 0 (higher density)\n\nFig: 23.8\n\n1 2 Generation\n\nWhen this hybrid duplex replicated in second round of replication, it contributed \"N strand to form another hybrid duplex and \"N strand to form a light duplex containing both \"N strands that is why this sample formed two sediments. On the basis of above mentioned results, they claimed that the DNA replication is sem iconservative.",
