        "heading": "23.7.1 Importance of gene regulation:",
        "headingUrdu": "موضوع 26",
        "text": "23.7.1 Importance of gene regulation:\n\nRegulation of gene expression (or gene regulation) is essential for prokaryotes and eukaryotes as it increases the versatility and adaptability of an organism by allowing the cell to express protein when needed. Furthermore, gene regulation drives the processes of cellular differentiation and morphogenesis, leading to the creation of different cell types in multicellular organisms where the different types of cells may possess different gene expression profiles though they all possess the same genome sequence.",
        "paras": [
          "23.7.1 Importance of gene regulation:",
          "Regulation of gene expression (or gene regulation) is essential for prokaryotes and eukaryotes as it increases the versatility and adaptability of an organism by allowing the cell to express protein when needed. Furthermore, gene regulation drives the processes of cellular differentiation and morphogenesis, leading to the creation of different cell types in multicellular organisms where the different types of cells may possess different gene expression profiles though they all possess the same genome sequence."
        ],
