        "text": "27.4.2 Importance of domestic animals:\n\nOn the basis of utility, domestic animals are categorized into the following functional groups:\n\n• Milk yielding animals (Cattle, buffalo, goat, sheep, and etc.).\n\n• Draught animals (used for load Bullock, horse, donkey, mule, bearing camel, elephant, yak etc.)\n\n• Fibre, hide and skin yielding Sheep, goat, cattle, buffalo, camel etc.\n\nMeat and egg yielding animals Fowl (hen)\n\nand duck, goat, buffalo, etc.",
